  "comments": [
    "Dictionary for course prose and site copy. Split into two kinds of entry:",
    "genuine domain vocabulary (Bitcoin terms, Austrian-school economics terms,",
    "author names, place names) and tokenizer artefacts. CSpell splits camelCase",
    "and PascalCase identifiers, so 'SearchDialog' yields 'earch' and 'attributes'",
    "yields 'ttributes'. Those fragments are listed so the checker stays usable;",
    "they are not words anyone writes."
